# REQUIRES: python-api, cuda
# Reporters of a Python simulation on a GPU (D207): the
# energy file and the trajectory of `mdir run`, written inside the parts of
# a run, against those of `mdir run`; the schedule; callbacks; the state
# unchanged by the reports; backups and refusals.
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_reporters.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide GPU mdir %t | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: GPU NVE Double dcd: 11 rows
# CHECK: GPU NVT Double xtc: 11 rows
# CHECK: GPU NVT Mixed xtc: 11 rows
# CHECK: GPU constraints, energies every 10, frames every 50: 11 rows with the optimal temperature equal to mdir run's
# CHECK: GPU constraints, energies every 20, frames every 10: 6 rows with the optimal temperature equal to mdir run's
# CHECK: schedule: callbacks at [(7, 7), (11, 11), (7, 14), (7, 21), (11, 22), (7, 28)]
# CHECK: a callback error ends the run at step 5
# CHECK: reports change no bit of the state in the deterministic mode
# CHECK: backups and refusals passed
